	website = {https://www.ren21.net/gsr-2024/modules/energy_demand},
	abstract = {Despite a notable decline in the prices of fossil fuels and other energy commodities in the first half of 2023, wholesale electricity prices remained high in many countries, negatively affecting energy-consuming sectors.

Inflation and high interest rates  continued to hamper investment, particularly in emerging markets that face debt burdens  and a higher cost of capital.

